        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify that thenable .then() must not be async]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42709</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42709"/>
        <updated>2026-01-09T15:05:17.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169272761?u=216904e59fc878dca16fb27b4b0450d5e5b69120&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR clarifies the requirements for implementing thenables in the Promise documentation, explicitly noting that a thenable’s <code class="notranslate">.then()</code> method must not be <code class="notranslate">async</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">A warning and example have been added to explain how using <code class="notranslate">async</code> can cause thrown errors to escape Promise error handling, leading to unexpected behavior during Promise resolution.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The Promise specification expects thenables to signal fulfillment or rejection synchronously, either by throwing or by explicitly calling the rejection handler. Using an <code class="notranslate">async</code> function for <code class="notranslate">.then()</code> violates this expectation because <code class="notranslate">async</code> functions always wrap errors in a returned Promise.</p>
<p dir="auto">This change helps readers avoid subtle bugs when implementing custom thenables and aligns the documentation with the actual Promise resolution semantics.</p>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #42193.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3684084966" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42193" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42193/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42193">#42193</a></p>]]></content>
