        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update CredentialsContainer.get() exceptions to reflect AbortSignal.reason]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42703</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42703"/>
        <updated>2026-01-10T05:53:55.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44868357?u=eac4520e2d0d57e1c2e4b3aca7febc9143729754&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">Updated the <code class="notranslate">CredentialsContainer.get()</code> documentation to accurately describe the behavior when an <code class="notranslate">AbortSignal</code> is triggered with a custom reason.</p>
<p dir="auto">Current documentation suggests only a generic <code class="notranslate">AbortError</code> is thrown, but per the spec and browser implementation, the promise rejects with the value of <code class="notranslate">AbortSignal.reason</code>.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Changes</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Parameters</strong>: Updated the <code class="notranslate">signal</code> option description to mention that rejection uses the signal's <code class="notranslate">reason</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Exceptions</strong>: Revised the <code class="notranslate">AbortError</code> entry to explain that the rejection value mirrors <code class="notranslate">AbortSignal.reason</code> (which defaults to <code class="notranslate">AbortError</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Examples</strong>: Added a new example demonstrating how to handle a custom string reason (e.g., "TimeoutError").</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<ul dir="auto">
<li>Verified the behavior against the <a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#abortsignal-abort-reason" rel="nofollow">WebIDL/DOM specification</a>.</li>
<li>Verified that the logic aligns with the existing documentation for <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal/abort_static#reason" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">AbortSignal.abort()</code></a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>

